{"seq":17,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T10:22:46.655Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"c10851a0243ca8f4960451e9263c702a9b91056ba662b17cb5cb88a2252a3cc2","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes. Two QFL ticket numbers turn up:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because the gatehouse kiosk wasn't sending SMS bay assignments to drivers on the 04:00 shift at Eau Claire, Doors 14-18. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that it was fixed. The action list also says to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThe other Moss notes have no QFL ticket numbers. The 9/14 North pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in mention QFL but cite no ticket. #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central notes belong to Central accounts, not QFL.\n\nTwo more QFL tickets are outside Moss's notes, in case you want them: #4912 (Gate_Dwell_Daily lag at Superior, Bay 14) is on the QFL account profile, and #8841 (carrier portal timeout on CSV uploads) is in your own 9 Apr renewal debrief notes."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":18,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T10:22:52.638Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7f0a093bf333d9621ad1607f92c041735e7ac47c81a35a0836ba94b4744fba17","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent you the list in our DM.\n\n1. #PD-4492 is in \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (5 Oct 2025). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers on the 04:00 shift at the Eau Claire yard, Doors 14–18, weren't getting SMS bay assignments from the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the next 04:00 shift went through without manual help. The note also says to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window, which is today.\n2. #4419 is in \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (undated). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss has six notes in all. The other four have no Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets. The 9/14 North pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in mention the account but give no ticket number. #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in the two Central team notes, but they belong to Central team accounts.\n\nI also told you about two more Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets that aren't in Moss's notes:\n- #4912, on the account profile: the Gate_Dwell_Daily report is lagging for Bay 14 check-ins at the Superior yard.\n- #8841, in your own 9 Apr renewal debrief: the carrier portal times out when uploading manifest files over 600 rows."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
